Let me try answering these questions:

{quote}how critical is this software for Bolt ?{quote}

It’s a very critical part of our infrastructure.


{quote}For what purposes we’re using it ?{quote}

JFrog is used to store and serve artifacts. Artifacts are virtual packages that contain source code compiled for testing and execution of our backend microservices. This software is deployed on the cloud infrastructure and runs our live services. In addition, the InfoSec team’s systems use JFrog to scan the artifacts and detect potential harmful software and security deficiencies.

Every time our engineers release new features and fixes to the production environment, JFrong’s artifactory service is used to store and deploy these changes.

