Analysis is complete, data can be found here under “Broken battery analysis” tab - [https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1g8SMx3Dbmm2hg6E86u-2IMfliwuEBRdhp2dUSIWBScA/edit?usp=sharing|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1g8SMx3Dbmm2hg6E86u-2IMfliwuEBRdhp2dUSIWBScA/edit?usp=sharing|smart-link] 

h2. Summary of broken HW13 batteries

18 batteries with different errors were brought to HQ for deeper analysis. The primary goal of this analysis was to understand if water sensors are working as they should or if water ingress errors were being falsely triggered.

The faults were as followed:

* 8 had signs of water damage, 3 of which the water damage was present throughout the whole corepack;
* 5 had a broken nickle tabs;
* 2 had loose ID pins;
* 2 had problems with BMS init;
* 1 had a broken charging port.

h2. Water ingress - E536, E537

7 of the 18 batteries had reported water ingress in past logs. All of these batteries had signs of water on the sensors. This is a good sign that water sensors are working as they should, reporting water ingress problems only if there is actually water present. More batteries with these errors should be inspected to confirm these results. One battery with severe water damage didn’t report the errors, this BMS will be analysed once a [BMS fixture|https://taxify.atlassian.net/browse/C2-348?atlOrigin=eyJpIjoiNjEwOTEzMTI2NTE0NDE0YzhhY2NkNDJlOTEyZjdkMzIiLCJwIjoiaiJ9] is ready.

Currently, there are approximately 10 additional batteries in Tallinn reporting water ingress. I am in the process of arranging their transfer to HQ for further analysis.

