I don’t mean only XTALs as considerations. For example the following line:

{quote}CUs use higher baud rate (460800) to communicate to GNSS which cannot be supported by esp32 UART in DFS.{quote}

This is a good consideration to be aware of when deciding components and which protocol to use.

Sending following byte string will be handled in IOT as unsolicited message and the scooter firmware versions are printed out in the same format as for Dragon:

{{5A A5 F0 01 3B 00 00 00 00 00 00 FC D2 02 1B 9C 14 80 06 8D 57 89 9A 18 DF 05 91}}

It is important to understand that the same interface is constantly used by IOT to poll all the devices on RS-485. Therefore:

* sending this command will temporarily disrupt the communication with other components
* IOT has high probability to miss the messages, so it must be sent multiple times until IOT is able to receive it and reply with an answer. 

For example HTerm can be used to send the message.



IOT replies with one of these (the numerical values are examples):

# If ECU and BMS functional: {{IOT FW: 0.9.1856-6a4f2cb5; ECU FW: 190; BMS FW: 035}}
# If ECU communication is not working:{{IOT FW: 0.9.1856-6a4f2cb5; ECU FW: ; BMS FW: 035}}
# If BMS communication is not working:{{IOT FW: 0.9.1856-6a4f2cb5; ECU FW: 190; BMS FW: }}

